From 2b28e8260ddad88b4b2f523c930842d7a62c6140 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:29:35 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] kcm_about-distro: hardware rows filled in after the first
 frame (GPU probe in a thread), Kirigami.FormLayout
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: Form/info (docs/page-design.md): distro header and Software first, then Hardware. Copy Details, Launch
Information Center, Show/Copy serial, the kcm-about-distrorc keys and the dump mode are unchanged. NOT BUILT YET (owner
stopped heavy work); checked statically only.

Moved / renamed:
- Kirigami.Form/FormGroup/FormEntry -> one Kirigami.FormLayout with noun sections "Software" and "Hardware"; each row is
  a label + value (+ hint badge, help button, Show button) as before. No label changed, so no aliases needed. "Reading
  hardware…" busy indicator after 150 ms. (HIG-001/005: state first; design §2, §7.)
- Relabel table inventory/relabel/kcm_about-distro.tsv (outer repo). 27 inventory rows kept (ksr markers in main.cpp and
  main.qml); inventory_check --kcm kcm_about-distro --strict: 0 lost.

Speed (cause found in code): the constructor called load() -> loadEntries() synchronously (bug 366158 asked for that so the
page never looks half-empty). That ran, before the page existed: ThirdPartyEntry scripts (two QProcess + waitForFinished
each), Solid::Device::listFromType + udev (CPUEntry, MemoryEntry), GPUEntryFactory::factorize(): the Vulkan and EGL helper
processes with waitForFinished(2 s) each, and an OpenGL context as the last resort (GPUEntryFactory.cpp:45-54).
Now: OS name/version and the cheap software rows are read in the constructor (first frame shows the state); then from
QTimer::singleShot(0) the third-party rows, CPU/memory, the dmidecode KAuth job and device-tree files are added, and the
GPU probe runs in a QThread (factorize(Fallback::No), entries moved to the GUI thread; the OpenGL fallback stays on the
GUI thread, GPUEntryFactory::fallbackEntries()). GPU rows are inserted right after Memory (same order as before; the
clipboard text keeps that order). "dump" mode still builds everything synchronously.
After numbers: pending, manager will measure.

Not built yet; uncertain: Kirigami.FormData.buddyFor on a RowLayout delegate of a Repeater; QThread::create lambda writes
m_gpuResult and the queued finished() reads it (destructor waits for the thread); the hardware busy flag ends with the
GPU probe, the dmidecode rows may arrive a bit later (as before).

